{%- doc -%}
  Category eyebrow for a product card (e.g. "SAUCES & CHUTNEYS"), used only
  on the occasion collection template (templates/collection.occasion.json) —
  scoped there deliberately, not sitewide. See ARCHITECTURE.md.

  Not a generic `text` block bound to a dynamic source: `{{ closest.product.type
  }}` was tried earlier this project and rejected outright by Shopify's own
  template validator (a real sync error, not assumed) — dynamic sources on a
  text block's setting are checked against a fixed allow-list, and product
  type/vendor aren't on it. This block reads `closest.product` directly in
  compiled Liquid instead, which isn't subject to that same editor-bound
  validation.

  Also not actually built on `product.type` even though that's the
  conceptually obvious field — confirmed live via /products.json that
  `product_type` is empty on every product on this store. `vendor` is just
  "Lambruk Pantry" on every product too. `tags` is the one field that
  reliably carries a real category (`tea` / `condiments` / `pantry`) — it's
  already the whole basis of blocks/lambruk-tag-filter.liquid, so this block
  reuses that same tag set and the same case-insensitive matching, and the
  same display labels, so the two stay consistent. A product with none of
  the three known tags renders nothing rather than guessing.

  The design's example copy ("SAUCES & CHUTNEYS · 260G") also includes a
  size suffix. Left out on purpose: sizes aren't a separate structured
  field on this store's products (all variants are "Default Title"; the
  size lives in the product's own title text, e.g. "Iced Tea 60g Loose
  Leaf") — extracting it would mean regex-guessing against free-text
  titles with inconsistent formats, not reading real data.
{%- enddoc -%}

{% liquid
  assign label = nil
  for tag in closest.product.tags
    assign downcased_tag = tag | downcase
    case downcased_tag
      when 'tea'
        assign label = 'Tea'
      when 'condiments'
        assign label = 'Sauces & Chutneys'
      when 'pantry'
        assign label = 'Pantry & Gifts'
    endcase
  endfor
%}

{% if label %}
  <p
    class="product-category-label spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: block.settings %}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {{ label }}
  </p>
{% endif %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .product-category-label {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: var(--text-3-size);
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #A07037;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.product_category_label",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-start",
      "label": "t:settings.left",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-end",
      "label": "t:settings.right",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
